{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "c3c534be-fb7c-503f-a4fe-b929b5b859e1",
  "Description": "A motorised paddle on a fixed hub sweeps 80 balls off its circle.\n\nThe hub is a Kinematic [RigidBody], which makes it a fixed point a joint can attach to. A Hinge [RigidJoint] with MotorSpeed turns the paddle around it. The paddle is heavy, so the balls cannot stop it.\n\nAKA: motor, spinner, turnstile, hinge, kinematic anchor\n\nTips\n- Animate MotorSpeed to speed the paddle up, stop it or reverse it.\n- LinearDamping on the balls stands in for rolling resistance and keeps them on the floor.\n- The hub and paddle share a CollisionGroup, or their overlap would push them apart.",
